# Build
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
# `go build ./cmd/<name>` writes its binary into the working directory rather than into /bin, so
# each one is named here. Without this a stray build lands in a commit, which is how a 30 MB
# `restore-drill` very nearly did.
/hubtask
/hubtask-migrate
/restore-drill

# Dependencies
/vendor/
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# JavaScript build output (ADR-0027). The two deliberate exceptions are un-ignored where they
# stand: presentation/webui/dist/index.html, so that go:embed resolves without a frontend build
# (ADR-0028), and core/domain/model/shared/LabelTokens.go, which is generated into the core and
# is not under any of these paths at all (ADR-0029).
apps/*/dist/
packages/*/dist/
.svelte-kit/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key
!deploy/docker/.env.example

# Tools
/.tools/
coverage.*
/tmp/
# scripts/gate-selftest.sh writes its violating packages here and removes them again; the entry
# is the safety net for a hard abort.
**/gate_selftest/

# Editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# The embedded UI bundle. Everything the frontend build writes here is generated - except
# index.html, which is committed as a placeholder so that //go:embed resolves and `go build ./...`
# succeeds without Node.js (ADR-0028).
/presentation/webui/dist/*
!/presentation/webui/dist/index.html

# Local Claude Code tooling (launch configurations); session-specific, not project content.
.claude/
